	I usually don't try altar-camping until I've got enough of a
food reserve that I don't need to resort to food prayer, for pretty much
that exact reason. Also, you run the risk of being *given* the hammer -
and a prayer timeout to wait out - when what you really need is the food
prayer.

> Final question (in this thread at least): I have a wand of polymorph,
> but I don't know how many charges I have in it.  Is it worth it to try
> to polymorph my (large and sturdy) dog?

	I probably would.

	But if you want to play it safe, you could try taming a feral
pet-type with a tripe ration or edible corpse or whatnot, and polymorph
the new one instead. That way if you burn up all your charges without
getting anything that doesn't suck, you've still got your original pet.

	And if you get something really good and still have charges
left, you can keep it and take a shot at getting something really good
out of your current pet, too.

	Also note: I don't polypile, so my advice comes from the
perspective of someone who hasn't got anything better to do with
polymorph charges than play pet roulette.

